# The lesson panel at 800x600 (docs/LEARNING.md "The lesson panel"), on a tutorial of our own
# (tests/input/learn), under the input lock: the game's prompts and the panel's own Leave
# question stay over the panel even when it is dragged under them; a dragged panel places
# itself again when it would hide the next step's outline; the compact panel and More; the
# panel's keys and Shift+F1 (docs/BUILDING.md "Input scripts").
options --learn-dir=tests/input/learn --tutorial=panel-check --layout=800x600 --size=800x600

wait-lesson panel-check
wait-for tag:lesson:panel
# 1 An explanation step shows the whole panel (its Less button makes it compact).
assert-present tag:lesson:leave
# Its Leave question: the panel dragged over the middle of the screen, the question over it.
drag tag:lesson:panel@60,12 to at:250,200
click tag:lesson:leave
wait-for item:No in="Leave Lesson"
assert-inside item:No in="Leave Lesson" tag:lesson:panel
screenshot leave-over-panel.png
click item:No in="Leave Lesson"
wait-gone item:No in="Leave Lesson"
assert-lesson panel-check
# Next by key (Alt+N); Back by key shows step 1 again (Back is dim there), Alt+N returns.
key Alt+N
wait-step 2
key Alt+B
wait 2
assert-disabled item:Back in=lesson
key Alt+N
wait 2
assert-enabled item:Back in=lesson
assert-step 2
# 2 An action step on a small screen: the compact panel, without Hide, Free Play and Leave.
assert-present tag:lesson:more
assert-absent tag:lesson:leave
screenshot compact.png
# More shows the whole panel; Less the compact one again.
click tag:lesson:more
wait-for tag:lesson:leave
screenshot more.png
click tag:lesson:more
wait-gone tag:lesson:leave
# Shift+F1 opens the manual under the lock; Esc closes it. Alt+R opens the step's page.
key Shift+F1
wait-window manual
key Escape
wait-closed manual
key Alt+R
wait-window manual
assert-present item:page:notes
key Escape
wait-closed manual
click item:next in=tag:cycle:ship
wait-step 3
# 3 Fleet Transfer.
click tag:order:fleet-transfer
wait-window fleet-transfer
wait-step 4
# 4 The whole panel, dragged over the middle of the screen, where Create Fleet asks for a name:
# the prompt lies over the panel, and its OK works.
click tag:lesson:more
wait-for tag:lesson:leave
drag tag:lesson:panel@60,12 to at:250,300
click tag:fleet-transfer:create-fleet
wait-for item:OK in="Create Fleet"
assert-inside item:OK in="Create Fleet" tag:lesson:panel
screenshot create-fleet-over-panel.png
click item:OK in="Create Fleet"
wait-step 5
# The panel keeps the place it was dragged to: it hides nothing step 5 outlines.
assert-inside at:300,350 tag:lesson:panel
# 5 Dragged over step 6's button (Planets, top left): when step 6 comes, the panel places
# itself again, and the button can be clicked.
drag tag:lesson:panel@60,12 to at:150,20
assert-inside tag:command:planets tag:lesson:panel
key Escape
wait-closed fleet-transfer
wait-step 6
wait 3
click tag:command:planets
wait-window planets
wait-step 7
# 7 Colonizable.
click tag:planets:colonizable
wait-step 8
# 8 Send Colony Ship: the panel dragged under where the list's Colonize comes; it lies over it.
click tag:lesson:more
wait-for tag:lesson:leave
drag tag:lesson:panel@60,12 to at:250,420
click tag:planets:send-colony-ship
click item:* in="Select Planet to Colonize"
assert-inside item:Colonize in="Select Planet to Colonize" tag:lesson:panel
screenshot colonize-over-panel.png
click item:Colonize in="Select Planet to Colonize"
wait-step 9
# 9 Finish by key.
key Alt+N
wait-result done
